WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.293
Week 15: Health, Body, and Emergencies. describe symptoms understand basic medical questions request urgent help

2
00:00:08.293 --> 00:00:15.796
Cultural lens. Pharmacies, clinics, emergency services, insurance, and expectations of formality.

3
00:00:15.796 --> 00:00:27.889
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.889 --> 00:00:39.683
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.683 --> 00:00:48.725
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:48.725 --> 00:01:12.529
Model language. Me duele mucho la cabeza. — My head hurts a lot. Tengo fiebre desde ayer. — I have had a fever since yesterday. ¿Es alérgico a algún medicamento? — Are you allergic to any medication? Llame a una ambulancia. — Call an ambulance. Se cayó y se lastimó el brazo. — He or she fell and hurt an arm.

7
00:01:12.529 --> 00:01:22.427
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
